// The port of listen() must be an integer, and an integer is an Int or an
// integer-valued Number (spec/05-stdlib.md, Integer arguments). `0i` asks the
// operating system for a free port as `0` does, so the Server binds one. A
// fractional port is a runtime error that halts the program.
// COVERS: integer-arg listen-port
// STATUS: error
// TIMEOUT: 10
// CHECK: true
var l = listen("127.0.0.1", 0i);
print l.port() > 0;
listen("127.0.0.1", 1.5);
print "unreachable";
